      "no": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I couldn't get tickets for London; it sold out in less than thirty seconds. But I managed to get three on resale for the",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 843
        },
        {
          "text": "Taylor's shows are girls' nights. It's the rules. And I don't really have my girls here",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1073
        }
      ],
      "words": 64
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Oh, I do know Talia. Maybe a little too well. But in spite of our history, and in spite of her being much closer to Ruth",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1444
        }
      ],
      "words": 37
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But my head and my heart feel torn and tangled right now, and for as much as I love my family, today is one of those day",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3080
        }
      ],
      "words": 38
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "His kind smile always fills me with ease. He's as close to me as my own father—growing up, he was always out working on ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4763
        }
      ],
      "words": 44
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Her husband grins at her, almost as lovesick as my brother and his wife, and a pang of sadness hits me out of nowhere. I",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5242
        }
      ],
      "words": 43
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Watching Brooks interact with his family—our family—it hits me. I've missed him. I've missed this. The way he loves his ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5454
        }
      ],
      "words": 28
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Neither Declan nor Jessa ever spoke nicely of their own families, and while they loved each other, the tiny community of",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5789
        }
      ],
      "words": 32
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "And the community I've always imagined myself in, the one I've always wanted",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5989
        },
        {
          "text": "it's what I've had all along. It's always been here. Coming home was exactly the reminder I needed",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6065
        }
      ],
      "words": 31
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I see Ruth smiling sadly as she watches Emmy's vegetable antics. Everett is holding her hand, resting them on the table ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8411
        }
      ],
      "words": 33
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Mom has mentioned before that Ruth can't have babies, but neither she nor Everett have said anything to me. If they want",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8774
        }
      ],
      "words": 42
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The way that, after everything that happened in New York, I'm afraid I might never have. I might never have the capacity",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9322
        }
      ],
      "words": 30
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Even Mom is suspicious, but when I lie and claim a headache, and duck out early back to my cabin, she just smiles sadly ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9606
        }
      ],
      "words": 39
    }
